				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-150224/scp-2558-j#post-648586</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 05 Dec 2009 00:21:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kimura Okagawa</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>398761</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Their cuteness rating is over 9000! *kickban'd from chat*</p> <p>Anyway, I have got to say, this and 914 are my two favorite SCPs on the site. The experiment between <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1011">SCP-1011</a> and 682 could also qualify as cute, but no one's released that security footage…</p> <p>I am kind of curious about the -Ex variety, though. When it says that they explode… is it like a small little boom, or a large blast? Also, how do they survive their own explosions? But most of all, I want to find out who the [REDACTED] thought putting one of these guys in 914 was a good idea. It's well-known what that thing does to organics (don't get me started about the 682 test), so who would want to do that to <em>any</em> kitten, let alone a 2558-J?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
